--TEST--
An unterminated string literal in a query given as a string literal is refused where it is written — `rule:core-classes/db-compile-time-query-checking`, ADR 0067 § 10
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The `'x` opens a string literal the text never closes, so the scan that
// counts placeholders reads every byte after it as being inside one and what
// the statement binds is what fits inside an opening quote rather than what
// was written. `nvs_db::sql`'s rewriter — the one the request itself would
// have run — refuses that text, which is what lets
// `rule:core-classes/db-compile-time-query-checking` make the same refusal here.
//
// It is a fact about the literal alone, so the params array beside it is never
// read: the `?` that looks like a placeholder is inside the open literal and
// binds nothing.
Core\Db\Connection $db = Core\Db::connect("main");
$db->query("select id from t where name = 'x and id = ?", [1]);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0769]: this text is not valid for this function: a string, a quoted name or a comment in this statement is opened and never closed. Everything after it is read as part of it, so the statement does not bind what you wrote
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
